/-!
# A formula for the different of a quasi-finite morphism of smooth schemes

Let `X` and `Y` be smooth of relative dimension `n` over a base `S` and let `f : Y ⟶ X` be a
morphism over `S`.  On an affine chart `V = Spec B ⊆ Y` over `U = Spec A ⊆ X` over
`W = Spec R ⊆ S` on which `Ω_{X/S}` and `Ω_{Y/S}` are free of rank `n`, the Kähler different of
`f` is generated by `∧ⁿ(df)`, the determinant of the matrix of `B ⊗_A Ω[A⁄R] → Ω[B⁄R]`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Discriminant.kaehlerDifferent_ideal_eq_span_det`: the ideal of the Kähler different
  over such a chart is generated by `∧ⁿ(df)`.
* `Stacks.Discriminant.exists_isAffineOpen_basis_kaehlerDifferential`: such charts exist around
  every point of a scheme smooth of relative dimension `n` over `S`, inside any prescribed open.
* `Stacks.Discriminant.exists_chart_kaehlerDifferent_ideal_eq_span_det`: **[Stacks, Tag 0BWJ]**,
  the local equation of `R`.
* `Stacks.Discriminant.exists_chart_kaehlerDifferent_ideal_eq_span_exteriorPower_map`: the same
  local equation with `∧ⁿ(df)` read as the map of rank-one top exterior powers it is.
* `Stacks.Discriminant.isLocallyPrincipal_kaehlerDifferent`: **[Stacks, Tag 0BWJ]**, `R` is a
  locally principal closed subscheme.
* `Stacks.Discriminant.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_kaehlerDifferent_of_etaleAt`:
  **[Stacks, Tag 0BWJ]**, `R` is an effective Cartier divisor when `f` is étale at the
  associated points of `Y`.
* `Stacks.Discriminant.nonempty_tensorIso_invertibleSheaf_kaehlerDifferent_of_etaleAt`
  (in `SmoothBundle.lean`): **[Stacks, Tag 0BWJ]**, the bundle identity
  `f^*Ω^n_{X/S} ⊗ 𝒪_Y(R) ≅ Ω^n_{Y/S}`.
* `Stacks.Discriminant.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_relativeDifferentials`,
  `Stacks.Discriminant.isInvertible_relativeDifferentialForms` and
  `Stacks.Discriminant.isInvertible_pullback_relativeDifferentialForms`: `Ω_{X/S}` has rank `n`,
  so `Ω^n_{X/S}` and its pullback are invertible — the three sheaves the tag's last assertion is
  about.

The same assertions for the different of [Stacks, Tag 0BW4] itself, for `f` locally
quasi-finite, are in `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Different/TheDifferent/SmoothDifferent.lean`.

## Implementation notes

The different of [Stacks, Tag 0BW4] is defined out of a relative dualizing module and a trace
element; the Kähler different of [Stacks, Tag 0BVW] needs neither, and the two are the same
ideal sheaf by [Stacks, Tag 0BWG].  The statements here are therefore about the Kähler
different, so that nothing beyond smoothness of `X` and `Y` over `S` is assumed.

Local quasi-finiteness of `f` is not among the hypotheses: the assertions below hold for any
morphism over `S` between schemes smooth of relative dimension `n`, because the only inputs are
that `Ω_{X/S}` and `Ω_{Y/S}` are free of rank `n` on small enough charts and that `Ω_{Y/X}` is
the cokernel of `f^*Ω_{X/S} → Ω_{Y/S}`.  It is needed for the tag's other two assertions.

Flatness of `f` — the first assertion of the tag — is
`Stacks.Discriminant.flat_of_locallyQuasiFinite`, in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Different/TheDifferent/SmoothFlat.lean`, which needs the local
quasi-finiteness that the assertions here do not.

### The bundle identity

The tag's last assertion, `f^*Ω^n_{X/S} ⊗ 𝒪_Y(R) = Ω^n_{Y/S}` as invertible sheaves, is proved
in `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Different/TheDifferent/SmoothBundle.lean`, as
`Stacks.Discriminant.nonempty_tensorIso_invertibleSheaf_kaehlerDifferent_of_etaleAt`.  Its
inputs:

* the three sheaves are invertible (`isInvertible_relativeDifferentialForms`,
  `isInvertible_pullback_relativeDifferentialForms`, and
  `Stacks.Divisors.invertibleSheaf_isInvertible` for `𝒪_Y(R)`), and `R` is an effective Cartier
  divisor (`isEffectiveCartierDivisor_kaehlerDifferent_of_etaleAt`);
* `∧ⁿ(df)` exists as a morphism of the first two, as
  `Stacks.Discriminant.topFormsMap`, and **in a chart both are trivialized and `∧ⁿ(df)` is
  multiplication by the local generator of the Kähler different**: this is
  `Stacks.Discriminant.exists_chart_trivialization_topFormsMap`, which also shrinks the chart
  into any prescribed open;
* **`∧ⁿ(df)` is a tensor product**: a morphism of invertible modules `φ : 𝒩 ⟶ ℒ` always factors
  as an invertible `ℳ`, a global section `σ` of `ℳ` and an isomorphism `𝒩 ⊗ ℳ ≅ ℒ` carrying
  `x ⊗ σ` to `φ(x)`, with `ℳ = 𝒩^{⊗ -1} ⊗ ℒ`.  This is purely formal, and it is
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorFactorization.exists_tensorFactorization`;
* given that factorization, the zero scheme of `σ` is `R`
  (`Stacks.Discriminant.zeroScheme_eq_kaehlerDifferent_of_tensorFactorization`), so `σ` is a
  nonzerodivisor section and [Stacks, Tag 01X0] (2) gives the stated identity:
  `Stacks.Discriminant.nonempty_tensorIso_invertibleSheaf_kaehlerDifferent_of_tensorFactorization`.

